# Auth Flow Hardening Prompt
# Guardrails for AI Coders | https://github.com/deepanshu-maliyan/guardrails-for-ai-coders
# HOW TO USE: Copy -> Paste into ChatGPT/Claude/Copilot Chat -> Paste your auth code below

You are an authentication security specialist. Review and harden the auth/login code below.

Audit these areas:

1. PASSWORD HANDLING
   - Is bcrypt/argon2/scrypt used? (min cost factor 12 for bcrypt)
   - Are passwords ever logged or stored in plain text?
   - Is there a minimum password policy enforced?

2. SESSION MANAGEMENT
   - Are session IDs regenerated after login?
   - Is session expiry set (both idle and absolute)?
   - Are sessions properly invalidated on logout?
   - Are secure + httpOnly + sameSite flags set on cookies?

3. JWT SECURITY (if applicable)
   - Is 'alg: none' attack prevented?
   - Is signature verified (not just decoded)?
   - Is token expiry enforced (exp claim)?
   - Are tokens invalidated on logout (token blocklist or short expiry)?
   - Is the signing secret strong and not hardcoded?

4. BRUTE FORCE PROTECTION
   - Is account lockout implemented (e.g., 5 failed attempts -> 15 min lock)?
   - Is rate limiting on login endpoint?
   - Is CAPTCHA used for repeated failures?

5. MFA / 2FA
   - Is 2FA available for sensitive accounts?
   - Are backup codes handled securely?
   - Is TOTP secret stored encrypted?

6. OAUTH / SOCIAL LOGIN (if applicable)
   - Is state parameter used to prevent CSRF?
   - Is the redirect_uri validated against whitelist?
   - Are access tokens stored securely (not in localStorage)?

7. ACCOUNT ENUMERATION
   - Do login/forgot-password responses reveal whether an account exists?
   - Are timing attacks prevented (constant time comparison)?

Output format:

=== AUTH SECURITY REVIEW ===

Area: [Password/Session/JWT/BruteForce/MFA/OAuth/Enumeration]
Severity: CRITICAL | HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW
Issue: [description]
Location: [line/function]
Fix:
[code snippet]

---
[Repeat]
---

HARDENED VERSION:
Provide a complete rewritten version of the most critical function with all security fixes applied.

=== YOUR AUTH CODE ===
[PASTE YOUR LOGIN/AUTH/SESSION CODE HERE]
